Graph"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/biconnectedComponents()":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The biconnected components, or blocks (Boost’s, NetworkX’s and igraph’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"biconnected_components"},{"type":"text","text":"): the maximal biconnected subgraphs, as sets of edges, which they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"partition (self-loops apart: a self-loop is in no block). Blocks are ordered by their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smallest edge position, each listing its edges in ascending position. An isolated vertex,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or one with only self-loops, is in no block. O(n + m)."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"biconnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BiconnectedComponents","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity21BiconnectedComponentsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/biconnectedcomponents()","kind":"symbol","title":"biconnectedComponents()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/biconnectedComponents()"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/isBiconnected":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isBiconnected"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isBiconnected","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the graph is biconnected (NetworkX’s, JGraphT’s and igraph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_biconnected"},{"type":"text","text":"): at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least two vertices, connected, and no articulation point. So K₂ is, and a graph with an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"isolated vertex is not. Stops at the first articulation point."}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isbiconnected","title":"isBiconnected"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/isBiEdgeConnected":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isBiEdgeConnected"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isbiedgeconnected","abstract":[{"text":"Whether the graph is bi-edge-connected (2-edge-connected; NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_k_edge_connected(G, 2)"},{"text":"): at least two vertices, connected, and no bridge. So a doubled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge is, and K₁ and K₂ are not. Stops at the first bridge.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isBiEdgeConnected","title":"isBiEdgeConnected"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","kind":"symbol","title":"Graph","abstract":[],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/bridges()":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"bridges"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/bridges()","abstract":[{"text":"The bridges: the edges whose removal adds a connected component (NetworkX’s, JGraphT’s,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"igraph’s and petgraph’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"bridges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), as positions in ascending order. A self-loop is never a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bridge, and neither is any of two or more parallel edges. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/bridges()","title":"bridges()"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/isConnected":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isConnected"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isConnected","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the graph has exactly one connected component; false for the empty graph, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isWeaklyConnected"},{"type":"text","text":" (igraph, JGraphT; NetworkX raises). Stops as soon as n − 1 joins have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"succeeded. Without flat rows, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"connectedComponents()"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directed.isWeaklyConnected"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isconnected","title":"isConnected"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/hasBridges":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Whether the graph has a bridge (NetworkX’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"has_bridges"},{"text":"). Stops at the first one found.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"hasBridges"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/hasbridges","kind":"symbol","title":"hasBridges","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/hasBridges"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity":{"title":"Connectivity","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity","abstract":[]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/connectedComponents()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"connectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity10ComponentsV","text":"Components"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedViewV","text":"DirectedView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">>"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/connectedComponents()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The connected components (NetworkX’s, Boost’s and igraph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"connected_components"},{"type":"text","text":"): in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the order of their first vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":", each listing its vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. The same value as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directed.weaklyConnectedComponents()"},{"type":"text","text":", computed over each edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once from flat rows ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidentIndexRows"},{"type":"text","text":"). Over a graph with vertex indices but without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them it is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directed.weaklyConnectedComponents()"},{"type":"text","text":": union–find over each row walked in place"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_forEachNeighborIndex"},{"type":"text","text":"), which a computed row (a product, a subgraph view) runs faster"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than copying the rows first. O(n + m α(n))."}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/connectedcomponents()","role":"symbol","title":"connectedComponents()"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/blockCutTree()":{"title":"blockCutTree()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/blockCutTree()","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/blockcuttree()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The block–cut tree (JGraphT’s "},{"code":"BlockCutpointGraph","type":"codeV